{
  "_comment": [
    "Which Microsoft service plans satisfy each controls.json LicenseRequirement.",
    "Source: Microsoft's 'Product names and service plan identifiers for licensing' reference (CSV) and the Microsoft Purview / Defender service descriptions.",
    "A rule is a list of groups; every group must be satisfied, and a group is satisfied by ANY one of its plans (AND of ORs).",
    "Plans are matched against Graph /subscribedSkus servicePlans with provisioningStatus 'Success', case-insensitively.",
    "'controls' overrides 'requirements' for one control: several controls share a requirement string but need different features (Customer Lockbox and Endpoint DLP are both 'M365 E5 or E5 Compliance add-on').",
    "Why this matters: Set-NRGLicenseGating takes a control out of the score when its requirement is NOT met, so a rule that misses a plan the tenant holds hides a real gap. Match the plan that delivers the feature, never the product name.",
    "The two 'E5 Compliance' requirement strings are the whole bundle (every feature their controls use); each control's own rule in 'controls' is what gating and the report use."
